Subject: [PATCH] volume OSD: themable colors via the screen view

The volume popup drew its gauge with the menu theme's Text/TextSmall
colors - grey-on-grey with the steamlike dark menu palette. Register a
'volumeInfo' element on the unified screen view (color = gauge fill,
backColor = track) so a theme can restyle it; unthemed behavior is
unchanged.

--- a/es-core/src/components/VolumeInfoComponent.h	2026-07-15 11:44:08.603271850 +0200
+++ b/es-core/src/components/VolumeInfoComponent.h	2026-07-15 11:45:04.399839344 +0200
@@ -4,6 +4,7 @@
 #include "GuiComponent.h"
 
 class ComponentGrid;
+class ThemeData;
 class NinePatchComponent;
 class TextComponent;
 class Window;
@@ -19,6 +20,10 @@
 
 	void reset() { mVolume = -1; }
 
+	// Optional colors from the current theme's screen view ("volumeInfo"
+	// element, color/backColor); falls back to the menu-theme greys.
+	void applyScreenTheme(const std::shared_ptr<ThemeData>& theme);
+
 private:
 	NinePatchComponent* mFrame;
 	TextComponent*		mLabel;
@@ -27,4 +32,8 @@
 
 	int mCheckTime;
 	int mDisplayTime;
+
+	unsigned int mBarColor;
+	unsigned int mTrackColor;
+	bool mThemedColors;
 };
